      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately, the existing state results in the system server failing to be able to utilize the IPsec tunnel mode APIs, for better or for worse.\n\nThis was a bug in that the above code was written expecting that the default appops mode was \"MODE_DEFAULT\" (and therefore it\u0027d check calling-or-self), and at some point the AppOpsManager code was checked in with MODE_ERRORED as the default. \n\nSince the MANAGE_IPSEC_TUNNELS permission is non-grantable, this should only succeed (not throw a SecurityException) if the caller is the system server (or we\u0027ve explicitly cleared the binder calling identity).",
