      "writtenOn": "2020-02-13T00:09:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not entirely. Since this is run on a serializing executor (as required by IKE),the following could happen:\n\n1. IKE sends a childTransformCreated (Outbound)\n2. IKE sends another childTransformCreated (Inbound)\n3. IKE sends the onChildOpened()\n4. The executor pulls the first queued job, and we fail to apply this transform in applyTunnelModeTransform() below, and therefore it triggers onSessionLost(), which shuts down the session.\n5. The executor pulls the second queued childTransformCreated. This should be ignored, since we\u0027ve torn down all other state, but haven\u0027t switched to a new Network.\n6. Similarly, the onChildOpened() must be ignored (otherwise we\u0027ll attempt to send traffic over a non-existent interface)",
      "parentUuid": "321e89fe_83f79f78",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2158,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 2159,
        "endChar": 76
      },
      "revId": "bfbe98780080f3ff645e03f334725e00cb25de6c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
